Subsequent factors are whether the monster is stunned, fleeing,
sleeping, or paralysed; a bonus for being an elf attacking an
orc; a penalty or bonus for being a Monk wearing or not wearing
armour; a penalty for being burdened or trapped; and then
the qualities (including, but not limited to enchantment) of
the particular weapon you're using, and your skill in it.

